<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:id "RSH-001" ; triage:sprint "c-2" ; triage:severity "BLOCKING" ; triage:location "crates/bd-cache-service/src/lib.rs:115" ; triage:source "qa-3 owning reviewer fenced JSON" ; triage:status "open" ; triage:record "{\"adr\": \"ADR-BDC-0016\", \"correlated_owner_ids\": [\"RSH-001\"], \"description\": \"C2 Application::shutdown at lib.rs:110-118 still stops admission/StopFlag and joins its cron task and real readiness worker. The cron task calls cron_run at :82, whose cron_run_hurried at cron.rs:198-224 awaits WorkerHandle::shutdown before ordinary expiry kill. Published sc-cron0.1.1 scheduler.rs:912-954 still waits task.await after deadline expiry, while worker.rs:539-550 awaits uncancelled blocking store work. sc-runtime0.1.1 builder.rs:342-344 correctly retains instance ownership until application cleanup returns. Therefore contended store work can extend the daemon cleanup/instance-lock interval beyond the approved finite bound. C1 RSH-001 remains OPEN at this concrete C2 occurrence; the independent readiness/test corrections do not change that public production shutdown API.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-service/src/lib.rs\", \"id\": \"RSH-001\", \"line\": 115, \"owning_sprint\": \"c-1\", \"remediation\": \"Keep C2 blocked on the existing C1/upstream bounded worker/store shutdown fix and qualify it through the actual daemon cleanup/instance-lock path after an authorized baseline is available. Preserve real owned joins and child reap before unlock; do not infer closure from happy-path tests, detach work through timeout/drop, relax the lifecycle bound or implement a local scheduler fork.\", \"reviewer\": \"arch-qa\", \"rule\": \"RULE-ADR-CODE\", \"severity\": \"BLOCKING\", \"status\": \"OPEN\", \"verification\": \"QA3: exact native crates tree, manifests/lock and governing architecture objects are byte-identical to QA2; concrete C2 occurrence directly rechecked, original owner ID retained.\"}" .
<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:occurrence "c-4@e7bafc2e5bdda1bf480823c7dd3ac73d0e16b702 qa-1" ; triage:occurrenceRecord "{\"category\": \"correctness\", \"evidence\": \"Independently read pinned sc-cron0.1.1 scheduler.rs904-949: timeout_at expires then task.await remains at930/948; worker.rs539-550 awaits uncancelled spawn_blocking store operation. Current Application shutdown joins that worker. Correlates existing RSH-001; no new contention execution claimed.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-service/src/lib.rs\", \"id\": \"RSH-001\", \"issue\": \"Existing upstream bounded-shutdown blocker remains reachable in current daemon cleanup; the passing uncontended Unix lifecycle case does not close it.\", \"line\": 115, \"recommendation\": \"Keep the owning C1/upstream blocker open until an approved published bounded worker/store shutdown API is adopted and the actual daemon instance-lock path is qualified under contention. Preserve owned joins; do not detach or weaken the bound.\", \"reviewer\": \"rust-qa-agent\", \"reviewer_records\": [{\"category\": \"correctness\", \"evidence\": \"Independently read pinned sc-cron0.1.1 scheduler.rs904-949: timeout_at expires then task.await remains at930/948; worker.rs539-550 awaits uncancelled spawn_blocking store operation. Current Application shutdown joins that worker. Correlates existing RSH-001; no new contention execution claimed.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-service/src/lib.rs\", \"id\": \"RSH-001\", \"issue\": \"Existing upstream bounded-shutdown blocker remains reachable in current daemon cleanup; the passing uncontended Unix lifecycle case does not close it.\", \"line\": 115, \"recommendation\": \"Keep the owning C1/upstream blocker open until an approved published bounded worker/store shutdown API is adopted and the actual daemon instance-lock path is qualified under contention. Preserve owned joins; do not detach or weaken the bound.\", \"reviewer\": \"rust-qa-agent\", \"severity\": \"critical\"}, {\"adr\": \"ADR-BDC-0016\", \"description\": \"Application shutdown awaits the real scheduler task, whose published0.1.1 shutdown/store path retains the known unbounded contended-store wait. ADR-BDC-0016 requires bounded worker cleanup before instance release. Correlates C2-REQ-004; positive uncontended/hook timings do not establish the total bound.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-service/src/lib.rs\", \"id\": \"RSH-001\", \"line\": 115, \"remediation\": \"Resolve the existing owning C1/upstream bound, consume the qualified parent and demonstrate the actual contended cleanup bound; do not drop a future/private handle as simulated shutdown.\", \"reviewer\": \"arch-qa\", \"rule\": \"RULE-ADR-CODE\", \"severity\": \"BLOCKING\"}, {\"evidence\": \"Independently inspected current service lib.rs:110-118 and cron.rs:198-224: ordinary expiry cancellation is invoked only after WorkerHandle::shutdown returns. Published sc-cron0.1.1 scheduler.rs:904-949 performs task.await after timeout_at; worker.rs:539-552 spawn_blocking store_call has no cancellable operation context. sc-runtime0.1.1 builder.rs:342-344 invokes cleanup before releasing stores/instance. Binding REQ-SERVICE-0003 and REQ-DAEMON-0004 require at-most2T and explicitly retain this open finding. The new Unix uncontended/canceled-read ownership fixture does not prove the contention bound.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-service/src/lib.rs\", \"id\": \"RSH-001\", \"issue\": \"The owned worker join can exceed the required total shutdown bound under contended blocking schedule-store work. Application::shutdown closes readiness admission and signals StopFlag, but its actual cron join cannot return within the advertised 2T when the pinned upstream worker is still inside an uncancelled store call. Runtime correctly retains its instance lock until that cleanup returns, so the same defect extends the instance-lock interval.\", \"line\": 115, \"recommendation\": \"Keep the existing C1/upstream RSH-001 and correlated C2-REQ-004 open. Consume an approved published cooperative store/worker shutdown API, integrate cancellation/deadline propagation without detaching owned work, and qualify actual daemon cleanup, lock retention/release and process-tree reap under controlled contention. Preserve the bound and existing join/ownership assertions.\", \"reviewer\": \"rust-service-hardening-agent\", \"severity\": \"critical\", \"topic\": \"graceful_shutdown\"}], \"severity\": \"critical\"}" .
<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:developerDisposition "upstream_pending" ; triage:developerDetail "C1/upstream: published bounded worker/store shutdown API plus actual contended daemon instance-lock qualification; retain joins and existing bound." .

